{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":90158,"duration_api_ms":144189,"num_turns":7,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"cbd54c2c-5158-411f-bf9e-613a3566fb10","total_cost_usd":0.4818457,"usage":{"input_tokens":449,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26694,"cache_read_input_tokens":81348,"output_tokens":2213,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26694,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":143,"outputTokens":8031,"cacheReadInputTokens":829937,"cacheCreationInputTokens":74778,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2167642,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":449,"outputTokens":2213,"cacheReadInputTokens":81348,"cacheCreationInputTokens":26694,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2650815,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All five amendments identify real, verified mass conservation defects in the tank simulation. CleanFilter and SiphonDetritus silently destroy N/C by reducing pools without routing removed mass. Shrimp reproduction creates mass from nothing. Conservation tests only cover the zero-DIC-rate case, missing the preset configuration. The budget tracking system lacks runtime conservation guards in release builds. Each amendment is well-evidenced and proposes a sound remediation path.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-3-d068d62d","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: CleanFilter reduces decomposer/nitrifier biomass by intensity*0.5 but the removed mass vanishes. The shrimp mortality code at shrimp.rs:483-491 demonstrates the correct pattern (routing dead biomass to fine_detritus via live_biomass_detrital_mass_g). CleanFilter should either route removed microbe biomass to detritus or record it as an explicit export in the budget ledger. This is a genuine N/C conservation violation."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-05e25271","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: ProcessParams::default() sets both DIC rates to 0.0, while default.toml sets respiration=0.08 and photosynthesis=0.12. The conservation tests use TankState::new() which gets the zero defaults, so they never exercise the DIC flux path that would break carbon conservation. Adding a comment or dedicated test acknowledging this is a low-cost, high-clarity improvement that prevents false confidence in conservation guarantees under realistic parameters."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-c9458760","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: SiphonDetritus multiplies particulate_organics_g_total and fine_detritus_g_total by (1-fraction) and returns None (no BudgetDelta). The removed mass is a physical export (siphoning waste out of the tank) that should be recorded. Either route to a BudgetDelta export classification or track as an explicit outflow. This is the same class of conservation violation as CleanFilter."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-77e36c27","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: At shrimp.rs:371-374, total_successful * 25 juveniles are added to juveniles_count with no mass debit. EggCohort tracks only count and progress_days—no biomass field exists. The existing hatch test only checks population counts, not mass. The existing budget test at budget_tracking.rs:404 explicitly sets hatch_success_base=0.0 to avoid this path. This is a clear mass creation violation that needs an egg biomass pool or explicit source debit, plus a regression test."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-a030e641","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: budget.rs:141 uses debug_assert! which compiles out in release. engine.rs:164-168 records and stores ticks but performs no conservation validation. The invariants.rs enforce_invariants function checks non-negativity and range clamping but not conservation laws. A tick-level conservation check (even test-only) would catch issues like the shrimp hatch mass creation immediately rather than relying on ad hoc test coverage. This is a sound defensive measure for a simulation where conservation is a core invariant."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"f39f4fca-70b8-4ed3-a788-31d380b1aa49"}
